      "question": "My manager wants a quick look at the oil condition on Transformer 1 at site MAIN. From the latest reading and the stats over the full available window, give me dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and say whether any of them moved in a direction that points to moisture ingress, air ingress or oil ageing. Rank the three concerns from most to least supported by the data. Don't use the combustible gases for this. If dielectric_rigidity or interfacial_v has no data, say so and base the ranking on oxygen and nitrogen only.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 (MAIN) — oil condition, non-combustible indicators** (5 readings, 2024‑01‑15 → 2024‑01‑19)\n\n| Parameter | Latest | Full-window mean (range) |\n|---|---|---|\n| dielectric_rigidity | 55 | 54.6 (53–56) |\n| interfacial_v | 45 | 45.0 (44–46) |\n| oxygen | 5850 ppm | 5822 (5700–5900) |\n| nitrogen | 27850 ppm | 27868 (27700–28000) |\n| dbds | 19 | 19.0 (18–20) |\n\n**Directional assessment**\n\n- **Air ingress:** Oxygen is at the upper end of its range (5850, near the 5900 max) and slightly above the mean; nitrogen is roughly flat at its mean. Combined, the elevated/slightly rising O₂ with high N₂ is the only signal even weakly consistent with air ingress.\n- **Oil ageing:** Interfacial tension (45) is at the low end of typical healthy values, and dbds (19) is mid-range rather than high — mildly consistent with ageing, but neither shows a downward trend over the window. Power factor (~1.0) and CO₂ are stable and unremarkable.\n- **Moisture ingress:** Not supported. Dielectric rigidity is at the top of its range (55, max 56) and water_content is at its minimum (0).\n\n**Ranking (most → least supported):**\n1. **Air ingress** — mildly supported by elevated, slightly rising oxygen alongside high nitrogen.\n2. **Oil ageing** — weakly supported by borderline interfacial tension; no confirming downward trend in dbds.\n3. **Moisture ingress** — essentially unsupported; dielectric strength is at its best value and water content is minimal.\n\nOverall the oil readings are remarkably flat over the five-day window; none of the three concerns shows a strong trend, so treat this as a \"stable, watch\" condition rather than an active degradation.",
